<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea to probe unfair trade in OTC market.</title>
<headline>S.Korea to probe unfair trade in OTC market.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea will begin investigating unfair trading in the over-the-counter (OTC) stock market in the second half of this year, the Securities Supervisory Board (SSB) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A statement said the move was being taken to help sound development of the OTC market.</p>
<p>South Korea revised its securities trade law in April as a step to regulate unfair trade.</p>
<p>The Korea Securities Dealers Association prepared the rules governing the market's operations and was now developing a system to examine sales and purchases.</p>
</text>
